# Zymbol-Lang Website License

This repository contains two kinds of work under two different licenses, matching
the split used by the interpreter repository: **code is AGPL-3.0-only, prose is
CC BY-SA 4.0.**

---

## Source Code — GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only)

All source code, including but not limited to:

- `src/zymbol/` — the browser engine
  - `zymbol.js` — hand-maintained JavaScript mirror of the Rust tree-walker
  - `zyp.js` — `.zyp` package reader (mirrors the `zymbol-package` crate's format)
  - `module-resolver.js` — module path resolution (mirrors `ModulePath::resolve_from`)
- `src/playground/` — playground UI (`playground.js`, `filestore.js`, `catalog.js`,
  `sidebar.js`, `highlight.js`)
- `src/site/` — landing-page logic (`main.js`)
- `worker/` — the Markdown negotiation Cloudflare Worker
- `tests/` — the test harnesses (`*.mjs`)
- the inline `<script>` blocks in the `.html` pages

**is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3.0
(AGPL-3.0-only).**

`src/zymbol/zymbol.js` is a hand-written port of the Rust tree-walker in
<https://github.com/zymbol-lang/interpreter>, which is AGPL-3.0-only. It is a
derivative work of that interpreter and carries the same license — it could not be
released under anything weaker.

Because the playground is a network-deployed application under AGPL section 13,
every page that runs this code links to its complete source at
<https://github.com/zymbol-lang/web>.

**Full License Text:** see [`LICENSE-AGPL-3.0`](LICENSE-AGPL-3.0) or
<https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html>

---

## Documentation, Examples & Design — Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)

All prose, teaching material and example programs, including but not limited to:

- `data/manuals/manual_*.md` — the compact manual in 110 languages
- `data/i18n/` — language metadata and showcase programs
- `examples/` — the example pool (`.zy` files, `.zyp` archives, `catalog.json`)
- `docs/` — engine parity notes, sharing guide, wiki article sources
- `*.md` at the repository root — `README.md` and the Markdown twin of each page
  (`index.md`, `install.md`, `playground.md`, `changelog.md`,
  `piqad-reference.md`), plus `llms.txt`
- the prose content of the `.html` pages

**are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
(CC BY-SA 4.0).**

Every manual carries the notice in its own footer, so a copy that travels alone
still says what it is.

**Full License Text:** see [`LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0`](LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0) or
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>

---

